& [IR4ImplementationProofCoverage] is the accepted behavior coverage for IR4 runtime graph implementation
  + [covered_behavior] is graph state and contract models validate missing authority, stale projection, hidden write attempts, node preconditions, edge contracts, and terminal outcomes
  + [covered_behavior] is checkpoint validation classifies current, stale, authority confusion, and false-readiness checkpoint cases without trusting checkpoint state as authority
  + [covered_behavior] is SOP-first interrupt context records ambiguous identity, authority conflict, contested coordination, stale input, missing proof, and forbidden context markers as generated projection packets
  + [covered_behavior] is pure graph runner returns terminal_success, terminal_blocked, terminal_stale, terminal_fault, or terminal_interrupt without external LangGraph dependency or live control APIs
  + [covered_behavior] is fixture runner loads only tracked fixture source and expected ledgers, compares all 10 accepted fixture cases, and refuses generated path escapes or source/expected-ledger mutation
  + [covered_behavior] is generated runtime reports are ignored, disposable, cleaned after tests, and excluded from authority discovery
  + [covered_behavior] is LangGraph dependency is deferred to a future explicit adapter activation slice while current proof remains dependency-free

  = must: require a future slice before widening fixture cases, output paths, dependency set, adapter APIs, or authority semantics

& [DownstreamIR5GateExport] is the downstream gate exported by this proof pack
  + [IR5_state] is may_open_only_after_IR4_implementation_completion_review_accepts_this_pack
  + [IR5_entry_model_route] is requires deeper reasoning for surface projection authority display conflicts and downstream readiness interpretation
  + [future_spark_suitable_work] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after IR5 slices define bounded surface fixtures, display rules, or deterministic projection checks
  + [future_langgraph_adapter_state] is gated_until_future_explicit_adapter_activation_slice
  + [safety_limit] is no operations control or live machine control authorized

  = must: open IR5 by minting or accepting downstream boundary work, not by directly adding surface runtime, queue, operations simulator, operations control, or live machine control
  = must: preserve IR4 runtime graph proof as boundary input for future surface, coordination, narrative, or adapter work

& [IR4ImplementationProofPackInvalidationRuleSet] is the staleness contract for IR4LangGraphProofRuntimeImplementationProofPackV1
  + [invalidated_by] is change to any accepted implementation output hash
  + [invalidated_by] is change to any accepted fixture source or expected-ledger hash
  + [invalidated_by] is change to generated-output proof or contract tests
  + [invalidated_by] is change to LangGraph adapter dependency decision
  + [invalidated_by] is change to IR4-IA01 through IR4-IA08 completion reviews that affects support, requirements, or gates
  + [invalidated_by] is generated projection promoted to source authority
  + [invalidated_by] is source fixture, expected ledger, source code, platform authority, or docs authority mutated by runtime code or tests
  + [invalidated_by] is dependency installation without authorizing slice
  + [invalidated_by] is operations control or live machine control leak

  = must: rerun IR4-IA09 or rebake the relevant surface after invalidation before downstream work consumes this proof pack
